<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Lintel — teaching, held and opened by those with the standing to decide</title>
  <meta name="description" content="A learning platform for institutions whose access to teaching depends on who the learner is — verified standing, not merely a paid enrolment.">
  <link rel="canonical" href="https://lintel.africa/">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#F5F4F1">
  <meta name="robots" content="index,follow">
  <!-- Open Graph / social sharing -->
  <meta property="og:type" content="website">
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="Lintel">
  <meta property="og:url" content="https://lintel.africa/">
  <meta property="og:title" content="Lintel — teaching, held and opened by those with the standing to decide">
  <meta property="og:description" content="A learning platform for institutions whose access to teaching depends on who the learner is — a verified, revocable standing conferred by a named authority.">
  <meta property="og:image" content="https://lintel.africa/og.png">
  <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
  <meta property="og:image:height" content="630">
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
  <meta name="twitter:title" content="Lintel — access to teaching, held and opened by those with the standing to decide">
  <meta name="twitter:description" content="A learning platform for institutions that guard their teaching. Access by verified standing, not merely payment.">
  <meta name="twitter:image" content="https://lintel.africa/og.png">
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 16 16'%3E%3Crect x='2' y='1' width='11' height='3' fill='%238A6D3B'/%3E%3Crect x='5' y='4' width='3' height='11' fill='%23161A2E'/%3E%3C/svg%3E">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/lintel.css">
  <style>
    /* Home-only layout. Extends the app's tokens; adds the threshold hero. */
    .home { --gutter: clamp(28px, 6.5vw, 44px); }
    .home-nav { position:sticky; top:0; z-index:50; background:var(--paper); border-bottom:1px solid transparent; transition:border-color .2s ease, box-shadow .2s ease; }
    .home-nav.scrolled { border-bottom-color:var(--rule); box-shadow:0 6px 22px -16px rgba(20,22,40,.4); }
    .nav-in { display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; padding:18px var(--gutter); max-width:1120px; margin:0 auto; }
    .home-nav .brand { display:inline-flex; align-items:baseline; gap:9px; font-family:var(--serif); font-size:21px; font-weight:600; }
    .home-nav .brand .mark { display:inline-block; width:15px; height:15px; position:relative; }
    .home-nav .brand .mark::before { content:""; position:absolute; left:2px; top:0; width:11px; height:3px; background:var(--brass); }
    .home-nav .brand .mark::after  { content:""; position:absolute; left:4px; top:3px; width:3px; height:12px; background:var(--ink-soft); }
    .home-nav .links { display:flex; gap:26px; align-items:center; font-size:14px; }
    .home-nav .links a { color:var(--ink-soft); }
    /* Hamburger — hidden on desktop, revealed on mobile */
    .nav-toggle { display:none; width:44px; height:44px; padding:0; border:0; background:none; cursor:pointer; align-items:center; justify-content:center; color:var(--ink); }
    .nav-toggle .bars, .nav-toggle .bars::before, .nav-toggle .bars::after { display:block; width:22px; height:2px; background:currentColor; border-radius:2px; transition:transform .2s ease, opacity .15s ease; }
    .nav-toggle .bars { position:relative; }
    .nav-toggle .bars::before { content:""; position:absolute; top:-7px; }
    .nav-toggle .bars::after  { content:""; position:absolute; top:7px; }
    .home-nav.open .nav-toggle .bars { background:transparent; }
    .home-nav.open .nav-toggle .bars::before { transform:translateY(7px) rotate(45deg); }
    .home-nav.open .nav-toggle .bars::after  { transform:translateY(-7px) rotate(-45deg); }

    .wrapc { max-width:1120px; margin:0 auto; padding:0 var(--gutter); }

    /* Hero — the threshold. A held door and an opened door, side by side. */
    .hero { padding:76px 0 64px; display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.15fr .85fr; gap:56px; align-items:center; }
    .hero .eyebrow { font-family:var(--mono); font-size:12px; letter-spacing:.14em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--brass); margin-bottom:20px; }
    .hero h1 { font-family:var(--serif); font-size:clamp(31px, 6vw, 52px); line-height:1.07; letter-spacing:-.015em; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 22px; text-wrap:balance; }
    .hero h1 .held { color:var(--held); }
    .hero h1 .open { color:var(--brass); }
    .hero .sub { font-size:18px; line-height:1.6; color:var(--ink-soft); max-width:46ch; margin:0 0 30px; }
    .hero .cta { display:flex; gap:14px; align-items:center; flex-wrap:wrap; }

    /* The doors figure — two thresholds, one held, one opened. Pure CSS/SVG. */
    .doors { display:flex; gap:22px; justify-content:center; }
    .door { width:130px; }
    .door .frame { border:2px solid var(--ink); border-bottom:none; height:210px; border-radius:4px 4px 0 0; position:relative; overflow:hidden; background:var(--paper-2); }
    .door .lintel-stone { position:absolute; top:-2px; left:-2px; right:-2px; height:16px; }
    .door.held .lintel-stone { background:var(--held); }
    .door.open .lintel-stone { background:var(--brass); }
    .door .leaf { position:absolute; bottom:0; width:100%; background:var(--ink); transition:none; }
    .door.held .leaf { height:100%; }
    .door.open .leaf { height:100%; transform:perspective(600px) rotateY(38deg); transform-origin:left; background:linear-gradient(90deg,#20263F,#161A2E); box-shadow:14px 0 26px -8px rgba(0,0,0,.25); }
    .door.open .glow { position:absolute; inset:0; background:radial-gradient(120% 90% at 100% 50%, var(--brass-soft), transparent 60%); }
    .door .tag { text-align:center; font-family:var(--mono); font-size:11px; letter-spacing:.1em; text-transform:uppercase; margin-top:10px; }
    .door.held .tag { color:var(--held); }
    .door.open .tag { color:var(--brass); }

    /* Belief strip */
    .belief { border-top:1px solid var(--rule); border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule); padding:44px 0; margin-top:20px; }
    .belief p { font-family:var(--serif); font-size:23px; line-height:1.5; max-width:30ch; margin:0 auto; text-align:center; color:var(--ink); }
    .belief p em { color:var(--brass); font-style:normal; }

    /* Capabilities — three, because the product genuinely has three primitives */
    .caps { padding:70px 0; display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr); gap:1px; background:var(--rule); border:1px solid var(--rule); border-radius:8px; overflow:hidden; }
    .cap { background:var(--paper-2); padding:32px 30px; }
    .cap .n { font-family:var(--mono); font-size:12px; color:var(--brass); letter-spacing:.1em; }
    .cap h3 { font-family:var(--serif); font-size:21px; font-weight:600; margin:14px 0 10px; }
    .cap p { font-size:14.5px; color:var(--ink-soft); line-height:1.6; margin:0; }

    /* Who it's for */
    .forwhom { padding:20px 0 76px; }
    .forwhom h2 { font-family:var(--serif); font-size:30px; font-weight:600; text-align:center; margin:0 0 8px; }
    .forwhom .lede { text-align:center; color:var(--muted); max-width:52ch; margin:0 auto 40px; }
    .whom-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr); gap:20px; }
    .whom { border:1px solid var(--rule); border-left:3px solid var(--held); border-radius:0 6px 6px 0; padding:22px 24px; background:var(--paper-2); }
    .whom h4 { font-family:var(--serif); font-size:17px; margin:0 0 8px; }
    .whom p { font-size:14px; color:var(--ink-soft); margin:0; line-height:1.55; }

    /* CTA band */
    .band { background:var(--ink); color:#EDECE9; border-radius:10px; padding:52px 48px; margin:0 0 80px; display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.3fr .7fr; gap:30px; align-items:center; }
    .band h2 { font-family:var(--serif); font-size:29px; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 10px; color:#fff; }
    .band p { margin:0; color:#B9BAC6; font-size:15px; max-width:44ch; }
    .band .actions { display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:12px; }
    .btn.brass { background:var(--brass); border-color:var(--brass); color:#fff; }
    .btn.brass:hover { background:#7A5F30; }
    .btn.onink { background:transparent; border-color:#3A3F58; color:#EDECE9; }
    .btn.onink:hover { background:#20263F; }

    .home-foot { border-top:1px solid var(--rule); padding:30px var(--gutter); }
    .home-foot .in { max-width:1120px; margin:0 auto; display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; gap:16px; flex-wrap:wrap; font-size:13px; color:var(--muted); }
    .home-foot .in .mono { font-family:var(--mono); font-size:12px; }
    .home-foot .flinks { display:flex; gap:20px; flex-wrap:wrap; }
    .home-foot .flinks a { color:var(--ink-soft); }

    /* Accessibility helpers */
    html { scroll-padding-top:76px; } /* in-page anchors clear the sticky header */
    .home { overflow-x:clip; } /* contain the opened-door transform without breaking position:sticky */
    .sr-only { position:absolute; width:1px; height:1px; padding:0; margin:-1px; overflow:hidden; clip:rect(0,0,0,0); white-space:nowrap; border:0; }
    .skip { position:fixed; left:12px; top:-48px; z-index:60; background:var(--ink); color:#fff; padding:10px 16px; border-radius:6px; transition:top .15s; }
    .skip:focus { top:12px; }

    /* Tablet & below — collapse the nav into a hamburger menu */
    @media (max-width:960px) {
      .hero { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:36px; padding:52px 0 40px; }
      .hero .doors { justify-content:flex-start; }
      .band { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:22px; padding:40px 34px; }
      .band .actions { flex-direction:row; flex-wrap:wrap; }
      .nav-toggle { display:inline-flex; }
      .home-nav .links {
        display:none; position:absolute; top:100%; left:0; right:0; z-index:30;
        flex-direction:column; align-items:stretch; gap:0;
        padding:6px var(--gutter) 18px; font-size:16px;
        background:var(--paper-2); border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);
        box-shadow:0 16px 30px -16px rgba(20,22,40,.28);
      }
      .home-nav.open .links { display:flex; }
      .home-nav .links a:not(.btn) { padding:14px 2px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule); }
      .home-nav .links a.btn { margin-top:14px; justify-content:center; min-height:46px; font-size:15px; }
    }

    /* Large phone — stack the card grids */
    @media (max-width:680px) {
      .caps, .whom-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr; }
      .belief { padding:34px 0; }
      .belief p { font-size:20px; }
      .caps { padding:44px 0; }
      .forwhom { padding:12px 0 56px; }
      .forwhom h2 { font-size:26px; }
    }

    /* Phone — drop forced line breaks, make CTAs full-width & thumb-sized */
    @media (max-width:520px) {
      .nav-in { padding:14px var(--gutter); }
      .hero { padding:36px 0 32px; }
      .hero h1 br { display:none; } /* let the headline wrap naturally instead of breaking mid-phrase */
      .hero .sub { font-size:16.5px; }
      .cta { flex-direction:column; align-items:stretch; }
      .cta .btn { justify-content:center; min-height:46px; }
      .band { padding:32px 22px; }
      .band .actions { flex-direction:column; }
      .band .actions .btn { justify-content:center; min-height:46px; }
      .doors { transform:scale(.82); transform-origin:left center; margin:-14px 0; }
      .cap { padding:26px 24px; }
    }

    /* Small phone — the doors are decorative; reclaim the space */
    @media (max-width:380px) {
      .hero .doors { display:none; }
    }

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) { html { scroll-behavior:smooth; } }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .door.open .leaf { transform:none; }
      .nav-toggle .bars, .nav-toggle .bars::before, .nav-toggle .bars::after { transition:none; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body class="home">
  <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
  <header class="home-nav">
    <div class="nav-in">
      <span class="brand"><span class="mark"></span> Lintel</span>
      <button class="nav-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="home-menu" aria-label="Menu"><span class="bars"></span></button>
      <nav class="links" id="home-menu" aria-label="Primary">
        <a href="/directory">Directory</a>
        <a href="#capabilities">How it works</a>
        <a href="#institutions">Who it's for</a>
        <a href="/directory" class="nav-signin">Find your institution</a>
        <a class="btn ghost small" href="/signup">Request access</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main id="main">
  <section class="wrapc hero">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">A learning platform for institutions that guard their teaching</div>
      <h1>Some teaching is <span class="held">held</span> <br>until you have the standing <br>to be <span class="open">let in</span>.</h1>
      <p class="sub">Lintel is a learning platform for institutions whose access to teaching depends on <em>who</em> a learner is — a verified, revocable standing conferred by a named authority — not merely on who has paid.</p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="btn brass" href="/signup">Request access</a>
        <a class="btn ghost" href="/directory">Browse institutions</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="doors" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="door held">
        <div class="frame"><span class="lintel-stone"></span><span class="leaf"></span></div>
        <div class="tag">Held</div>
      </div>
      <div class="door open">
        <div class="frame"><span class="lintel-stone"></span><span class="glow"></span><span class="leaf"></span></div>
        <div class="tag">Opened</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="belief">
    <div class="wrapc">
      <p>A door is not a paywall. It opens for the person who was meant to pass through — and for no one else, no matter what they paid.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrapc caps" id="capabilities">
    <h2 class="sr-only">How it works</h2>
    <div class="cap">
      <div class="n">01 · STANDING</div>
      <h3>Access by attestation</h3>
      <p>A named authority — an elder, an examiner, a registrar — confers a verified standing on a person. Teaching opens against that standing, and closes the moment it is revoked. Never granted by the software, never by a payment.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cap">
      <div class="n">02 · CONTENT</div>
      <h3>Delivery follows sensitivity</h3>
      <p>Restricted material is streamed, watermarked, and logged — never downloadable. Open teaching is free to save. The content's own policy decides how it may travel, per item.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cap">
      <div class="n">03 · JUDGEMENT</div>
      <h3>Assessment by people</h3>
      <p>Oral and video performance, graded against a rubric by named assessors, moderated where a senior voice must confirm a junior one. When a mark is overruled, both survive in the record.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrapc forwhom" id="institutions">
    <h2>Built for institutions a generic LMS can't serve</h2>
    <p class="lede">If your teaching is conditional on who the learner is — not just whether they enrolled — the primitives you need are the ones most platforms treat as an afterthought.</p>
    <div class="whom-grid">
      <div class="whom">
        <h4>Traditions with initiation</h4>
        <p>Sacred and cultural schools where certain teaching is held until a person is initiated, and an elder is the only one who can attest that they are.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="whom">
        <h4>Licensing and professional bodies</h4>
        <p>Colleges where a module on drug administration or clinical practice opens only to a learner holding a current, verified professional standing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="whom">
        <h4>Institutions of record</h4>
        <p>Any body that must prove — years later — who was admitted to what, who conferred a standing, and who awarded a credential. Every decision is logged, nothing is erased.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrapc">
    <div class="band">
      <div>
        <h2>Bring your institution's own rules.</h2>
        <p>Lintel holds no opinion about who deserves to learn what. It gives your authorities the means to decide, enforces their decision faithfully, and keeps the record. You write the rules; the platform keeps the door.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn brass" href="/signup">Request access</a>
        <a class="btn onink" href="/verify">Verify a credential</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  </main>

  <footer class="home-foot">
    <div class="in">
      <span>Lintel — access to teaching, held and opened by those with the standing to decide.</span>
      <nav class="flinks" aria-label="Footer">
        <a href="/directory">Directory</a>
        <a href="/verify">Verify a credential</a>
        <a href="/signup">Request access</a>
        <a href="mailto:hello@lintel.africa" class="mono">hello@lintel.africa</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </footer>
  <script>
    (function () {
      var nav = document.querySelector('.home-nav');
      var btn = nav && nav.querySelector('.nav-toggle');
      var menu = document.getElementById('home-menu');
      if (nav) {
        var onScroll = function () { nav.classList.toggle('scrolled', window.scrollY > 4); };
        onScroll();
        window.addEventListener('scroll', onScroll, { passive: true });
      }
      if (!btn || !menu) return;
      function setOpen(open) {
        nav.classList.toggle('open', open);
        btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', open ? 'true' : 'false');
      }
      btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
        setOpen(btn.getAttribute('aria-expanded') !== 'true');
      });
      // close on link tap, on Escape, and on outside click
      menu.addEventListener('click', function (e) { if (e.target.closest('a')) setOpen(false); });
      document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) { if (e.key === 'Escape') setOpen(false); });
      document.addEventListener('click', function (e) { if (!nav.contains(e.target)) setOpen(false); });
    })();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
